1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,200
R-LearnXR is an open-source framework for building reproducible
virtual data laboratories with R and Quarto.

2
00:00:08,200 --> 00:00:17,700
It turns an R data frame into a portable, browser-based 3D lesson,
without requiring a headset or an application server.

3
00:00:17,760 --> 00:00:26,680
Every lesson follows a clear learning cycle: predict a pattern,
rotate the data space, zoom, and select evidence.

4
00:00:27,080 --> 00:00:35,330
The same data are available in a semantic table, so keyboard users
can inspect an exact point without relying on the canvas.

5
00:00:35,740 --> 00:00:44,700
The learning companion keeps reasoning visible. A selected point
generates a coordinate-based observation.

6
00:00:44,700 --> 00:00:55,330
The learner must connect an axis and its direction to a claim
before moving to the transfer task.

7
00:00:56,040 --> 00:01:04,000
Responses remain in the browser, and the lesson can be restarted.
Authors continue to work in R and Quarto.

8
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:12,300
Automated checks cover deterministic seeds, locked environments,
data licenses, accessible alternatives, and learning-loop controls.

9
00:01:12,750 --> 00:01:20,100
The repository includes a reference lesson and a real PCA example
built with the palmerpenguins data.

10
00:01:20,110 --> 00:01:28,820
Both lessons are tested, rendered in continuous integration,
and designed for reuse by R educators and contributors.

11
00:01:29,350 --> 00:01:36,500
This MVP demonstrates the core grant value:
focused technical infrastructure and open educational practice.

12
00:01:36,500 --> 00:01:43,140
It provides a low-risk path from a working prototype
to a community-ready R package.

